# The {{DeviceBoundSessionsObserver}} interface # {#the-device-bound-sessions-observer-interface}

The {{DeviceBoundSessionsObserver}} interface can be used to observe {{DeviceBoundSessionsReport}}.

<pre class="idl">
[Exposed=Window]
interface DeviceBoundSessionsObserver {
  constructor(
    DeviceBoundSessionsObserverCallback callback,
    optional DeviceBoundSessionsObserverOptions options = {}
  );
  undefined observe();
  undefined disconnect();
  sequence&lt;DeviceBoundSessionsReport> takeRecords();
};

callback DeviceBoundSessionsObserverCallback = undefined (
  sequence&lt;DeviceBoundSessionsReport> reports,
  DeviceBoundSessionsObserver observer
);
</pre>

## {{DeviceBoundSessionsObserverOptions}} dictionary ## {#options-dictionary}

<pre class="idl">
dictionary DeviceBoundSessionsObserverOptions {
  boolean unbuffered = false;
  AbortSignal signal;
};
</pre>

<dl dfn-for="PerformanceObserverCallbackOptions" data-export>
  : unbuffered
  :: Foo
  : signal
  :: Bar
</dl>

## {{DeviceBoundSessionsObserver/observe()}} method ## {#observe-method}

<div algorithm>
  The <dfn export method for=DeviceBoundSessionsObserver>`observe()`</dfn> method instructs the user agent to register the observer and must run these steps:
</div>

## Report types ## {#report-types}

<pre class="idl">
enum DeviceBoundSessionsReportKind {
  "session",
  "registration"
};

dictionary DeviceBoundEstablishedSessionReport {
  required DeviceBoundSessionsReportKind type;
  required DOMString sessionOrigin;
  required DOMString sessionId;
  required DOMString refreshUrl;
  required DOMHighResTimeStamp creationTime;
};

dictionary DeviceBoundSessionRegistrationReport {
  required DeviceBoundSessionsReportKind type;
  required DOMString registrationUrl;
  required boolean success;
  required DOMHighResTimeStamp endTime;
  DeviceBoundEstablishedSessionReport session;
  DOMString reason;
  long? code = null;
  DOMString providerUrl;
  DOMString providerSessionId;
};

typedef (
  DeviceBoundSessionRegistrationReport
  or DeviceBoundEstablishedSessionReport) DeviceBoundSessionsReport;
</pre>

A <dfn export type><code>DeviceBoundSessionsReport</code></dfn> can be:

- A <dfn export dictionary><code>DeviceBoundEstablishedSessionReport</code></dfn>, representing a [=device bound session=].
- A <dfn export dictionary><code>DeviceBoundSessionRegistrationReport</code></dfn>, representing the outcome of [=create a session=].

# Algorithms # {#algorithms}

## Changes to [=create a session=] ## {#modification-to-dbsc-creation}

<div algorithm='create-a-session-change'>
  When [=create a session=] returns, the user agent must run these steps:

  1. Let |registration| be TODO (from the remote algo, might need more changes).
  1. [=list/For each=] |observer| in [TODO observers list]:
    1. Let |ESO| be |observer|'s [=relevant settings object=].
    1. If [=determine registration visibility=] returns "visible" for |ESO| and |registration|, call |observer|'s {{DeviceBoundSessionsObserver/constructor(callback)/callback}} with |registration| and |observer|, then [=iteration/continue=].
    1. If [=determine session visibility=] returns "visible" for |ESO| and |registration|'s {{DeviceBoundSessionRegistrationReport/session}}, call |observer|'s {{DeviceBoundSessionsObserver/constructor(callback)/callback}} with |registration|'s {{DeviceBoundSessionRegistrationReport/session}} and |observer|.
</div>

## Session reports visibility ## {#session-reports-visibility}

<div algorithm>
  <dfn export>Determine session visibility</dfn> returns "visible" when [=environment settings object=] |environment| is allowed to receive a report about [=device bound session=] |session|. Returns "hidden" otherwise.

  1. If |environment| is not a [=secure context=], return "hidden".

  1. Let |url| be |environment|'s [=environment/creation URL=].

  1. If |url| is not |session|'s [=device bound session/refresh URL=]:

    1. If the result of running [=algorithms/determine if a URL is in scope=] with |url| and |session| is false, return "hidden".

  1. Optional, TODO: pick one (or do both?)
    - Return [=check whether credentials would be included=] given |environment| and |session|.
    - If |environment| [=environment/has storage access=], return "visible".

  1. Return "hidden".
</div>

<div algorithm>
To <dfn>check whether credentials would be included</dfn>, given an [=environment settings object=] |environment| and a [=device bound session=] |session|:

  1. Let |url| be |environment|'s [=environment/creation URL=].

  Note: |url| can be reused from an earlier step if merged.

  1. Let |request| be a new [=request=] whose [=request/URL=] is |url|, [=request/method=] is \``GET`\`, [=request/client=] is |environment|, [=request/mode=] is "`same-origin`", and [=request/credentials mode=] is "`include`".

  1. [=list/For each=] |credential| of |session|'s [=device bound session/session credentials=]:

    1. If |credential|'s [=session credential/type=] is "`cookie`", and a cookie with |credential|'s [=session credential/attributes=] would be attached to |request| (see [[RFC6265#cookie]]), return "visible".

  1. Return "hidden".
</div>

<div class="example" id="session-visibility-example">

  Note, TODO: rework the example after rules rework (esp. hasStorageAccess())

  Given the following (incomplete) session definition:

  ```json
  {
    "session_identifier": "session_id",
    "refresh_url": "/refresh",
    "scope": {
      "origin": "https://example.com",
      "include_site": true,
      "scope_specification" : [
        { "type": "exclude", "domain": "untrusted.example.com", "path": "/" },
        { "type": "exclude", "domain": "*.example.com", "path": "/static" }
      ]
    },
    "credentials": [{
      "type": "cookie",
      "name": "auth_cookie",
      "attributes": "Domain=example.com; Path=/; Secure; HttpOnly; SameSite=Strict"
    }]
  }
  ```

  The following table illustrates whether `session_id` is visible to various execution environments:

  <table>
    <tr>
        <th>Creation URL</th>
        <th>Environment Context</th>
        <th>Visible?</th>
        <th>Reason</th>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td>`https://example.com/account`</td>
        <td>Top-level window</td>
        <td>`true`</td>
        <td>Secure, in scope, and `auth_cookie` attaches to same-origin requests.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td>`https://sub.example.com/app`</td>
        <td>Top-level window</td>
        <td>`true`</td>
        <td>Step 6: Permitted by `include_site`, domain matches `example.com`, same-site context.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td>`https://example.com/refresh`</td>
        <td>Top-level window or embedded frame</td>
        <td>`true`</td>
        <td>Step 3: Creation URL equals refresh URL, short-circuiting scope and cookie checks.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td>`https://example.com/account`</td>
        <td>Cross-site embedded frame (e.g., inside `https://other.org`)</td>
        <td>`false`</td>
        <td>Step 6: Request client is cross-site; `SameSite=Strict` blocks cookie attachment.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td>`https://untrusted.example.com/`</td>
        <td>Top-level window</td>
        <td>`false`</td>
        <td>Step 4: URL is excluded by the explicit `untrusted.example.com` rule in `scope_specification`.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td>`https://app.example.com /static/index.html`</td>
        <td>Top-level window</td>
        <td>`false`</td>
        <td>Step 4: URL path matches the `*.example.com` prefix exclusion rule for `/static`.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td>`http://example.com/account`</td>
        <td>Top-level window</td>
        <td>`false`</td>
        <td>Step 1: Insecure scheme; environment is not a secure context.</td>
    </tr>
  </table>

</div>

## Registration reports visibility ## {#registration-reports-visibility}

<div algorithm>
  <dfn export>Determine registration visibility</dfn> returns "visible" when [=environment settings object=] |environment| is allowed to receive a report about [registration attempt ref. TODO] |registration|. Returns "hidden" otherwise.
  
  1. If |environment| is not a [=secure context=], return "hidden".
  1. Let |observer key| be the result of running [=obtain a storage key for non-storage purposes=] given |environment|.
  1. If |observer key| [=storage key/equals=] |registration|'s [=report storage key=], return "visible".
  1. Return "hidden".
</div>

### Registration storage key ### {#registration-storage-key}

<div algorithm>

  Note: This algorithm takes [storage partitioning](https://privacycg.github.io/storage-partitioning/) into account.

  The <dfn export>report storage key</dfn> of a [registration attempt ref. TODO] |registration attempt| is defined as:

  1. Let |request| be |registration attempt|'s [TODO registration attempt/request].
  1. Let |environment| be [=request/determine the environment=] given |request|.
  1. Let |top-level site| be |environment|'s [=storage key/top-level site=].
     TODO: Too ill-defined?
  1. Let |origin| be |request|'s [=request/URL=]'s [=url/origin=].
  1. Return a [=storage key=] [=tuple=] consisting of the [=storage key/origin=] |origin| and the [=storage key/top-level site=] |top-level site|.
</div>


